# L §3.3 accrue: simple, p × r × dcf = 1000 × 0.12 × 181/365 = 4344/73 PLN; effective over a dcf of exactly 1
# (365 days, act365), p × ((1 + r)^1 - 1) = 120 PLN; nominal 12, p × ((1 + r/12)^12 - 1) = 1000 × 0.126825030131969720661201
# = 126.825030131969720661201 PLN.  "Nothing rounds": a num PLN.  The row lists simple, effective and nominal m only:
# discount is outside it (L §8.4: RUN-DOMAIN at the key).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input p: money PLN
input r: rate
input c12: compounding
input d1: date
input d2: date
input d3: date
def acs: num PLN = accrue(p, r, d1, d2, act365, simple) at reader
def ace: num PLN = accrue(p, r, d1, d3, act365, effective) at reader
def acn: num PLN = accrue(p, r, d1, d3, act365, c12) at reader
def acd: num PLN = accrue(p, r, d1, d3, act365, discount) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  p = 1 000.00 PLN
  r = 12 %/year
  c12 = nominal 12
  d1 = 2026-01-01
  d2 = 2026-07-01
  d3 = 2027-01-01

ask a: acs, ace, acn law 2026-06-30
ask b: acd law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: (4344/73 (59.5068493150685) PLN, 120 PLN, 126.825030131969720661201 (126.82503013197) PLN)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
b: refused: RUN-DOMAIN ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
